# Trivy ignore list (docs/architecture.md section 6.3). Read by every Trivy scan in CI
# (image scan in ci.yml, dependency scan and self-test in security.yml).
#
# Policy: a finding is ignored only when it is confirmed not to affect this project or no
# fixed version exists yet, and only temporarily. Every entry MUST have:
#   - a comment above it: package, why it does not apply / why it cannot be fixed now,
#     who accepted it and when, and the tracking issue or PR;
#   - an expiry date with `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` (Trivy stops ignoring it after that date).
# Entries without a reason or without an expiry date are not accepted in review.
#
# Example:
#   # example-lib 1.2.3 (backend): vulnerable code path not used; fix in 1.2.4 not released yet.
#   # Accepted by <owner> on 2026-11-01, tracked in #<n>.
#   CVE-0000-00000 exp:2026-12-01
#
# No accepted findings.
